[
    {
        "content": "<p>I'm looking at cleaning up <code>backward.privateInPublic</code>, and am wondering why a couple of <code>Hom</code>s are one-field structures with private constructors. This seems to necessitate <code>backward.privateInPublic</code> in the file due to reliance on defeq in the given file. What's the design motivating <code>private mk</code>?</p>",
        "id": 615081606,
        "sender_full_name": "Thomas Murrills",
        "timestamp": 1786053919
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Namely, if the goal is to avoid defeq abuse downstream, I'm wondering if we could instead use a pattern like</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">structure</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">CommMonCat</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Hom</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">CommMonCat</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">u</span><span class=\"o\">})</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"kn\">private</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">mkInternal</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">::</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"sd\">/-- The underlying monoid homomorphism. -/</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">hom'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span>\n\n<span class=\"kd\">@[</span><span class=\"n\">no_expose</span><span class=\"kd\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">CommMonCat</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Hom</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mk</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">CommMonCat</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">hom'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Hom</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mkInternal</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hom'</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>or if this is nonsense. <span aria-label=\"upside down\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f643\" role=\"img\" title=\"upside down\">:upside_down:</span></p>",
        "id": 615109489,
        "sender_full_name": "Thomas Murrills",
        "timestamp": 1786069864
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I think maybe the <code>private</code> means \"this is an implementatil detail because lean gets the argument explicitness wrong\"; that is, it's the old meaning of private not the new one</p>",
        "id": 615126747,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1786079854
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Aha, I think it is actually due to the motivation explained in <a href=\"#narrow/channel/287929-mathlib4/topic/Concrete.20category.20class.20redesign/near/493903980\">this message</a>.</p>",
        "id": 615284225,
        "sender_full_name": "Thomas Murrills",
        "timestamp": 1786135300
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>This makes me wonder if the instance fields calling <code>.mk</code> should be <code>:= private</code>? <span aria-label=\"thinking\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f914\" role=\"img\" title=\"thinking\">:thinking:</span> We still have defeq issues to be solved, though; I'm running into deterministic timeouts at <code>Iso.refl _</code> later on if I try the simple thing :)</p>",
        "id": 615285079,
        "sender_full_name": "Thomas Murrills",
        "timestamp": 1786135747
    }
]